Reports progress from Zucchini's long loops and between its steps, and stops them when the C API's
progress callback cancels. suffix_array.h, which generating, applying and suffix sorting all reach,
declares zucchini_rs::ProgressSteps, ProgressLoop and ReportProgress; shim/zucchini_c.cc defines
them, and they throw zucchini_rs::Cancelled, which the C API returns as ZUCC_CANCELLED. Patches and
results are unchanged, and so is speed: tight loops run in zucchini_rs::ProgressChunks, reporting
between chunks with their inner loops as they were, and ProgressLoop checks only loops whose every
pass already does far more work.

In a file another patch also changes, lines are added only below that patch's hunks, so it still
applies at the lines it states: ExtendEquivalenceForward, above vector-containers.patch's hunks in
equivalence_map.cc, reports nothing.

